---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import Grid from '../../components/Grid.astro';
import Card from '../../components/Card.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/CallToAction.astro';
import PhotoPlaceholder from '../../components/PhotoPlaceholder.astro';
import Figure from '../../components/Figure.astro';
import forecast from '../../assets/photos/wind-gust-forecast.jpg';
import { ORG, STORM } from '../../consts';
---
<BaseLayout
  title={STORM.name}
  description="What the Florida Lantern Project can help with during and after Tropical Storm Isaias — free documented inspections, aid navigation, connectivity, and a storm line answered by a person."
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow={`Active · as of ${STORM.asOf}`}
    title={STORM.name}
    lede={STORM.status}
    image={forecast}
    imageAlt=""
    size="tall"
  >
    <p class="actions">
      <a class="btn" href="/help/request">Request help</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/partner">Partner with us</a>
    </p>
  </Hero>

  <Section>
    <p class="urgent">
      <strong>If you are in immediate danger, call 911.</strong> We are not an
      emergency service and we are not monitored around the clock.
    </p>
    <p>
      Evacuation orders come from your county, not from us. Find yours at
      <a href="https://www.floridadisaster.org/">floridadisaster.org</a> and go
      when you are told to go. If your reason for staying is an animal, call us
      first — that is one of the most common reasons families don't leave, and
      it is a solvable problem more often than people think.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="surface" title="What we can help with">
    <Grid>
      {STORM.offers.map((o) => (
        <Card title={o.title}><p>{o.body}</p></Card>
      ))}
    </Grid>
    <p class="boundary">
      We are not insurance adjusters and we do not negotiate with your insurer.
      We inspect, we document, and we hand you the report.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Being honest about where we are">
    <p>
      We are based in Tampa. This storm is forecast for the Panhandle, six hours
      up the road, in counties where almost nobody has heard of us. Writing that
      on our own website is better than pretending otherwise.
    </p>
    <p>
      So the most useful thing we can do this week is not to arrive unannounced.
      It is to be reachable, to coordinate through county emergency management
      and 211 rather than around them, and to come back in the weeks afterward —
      when the news trucks have gone and people are still trying to get a roof
      documented and a claim moving. That is the part nobody covers, and it is
      the part we are actually equipped for.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are an organization up there with people who need help, the fastest
      route to us is the partner form. One message from a pastor is worth more
      than anything we could post.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="surface" title="After it passes">
    <PhotoPlaceholder
      subject="Aerial survey of storm damage along the Gulf Coast"
      source="To licence: Getty / AP editorial, or shoot it ourselves once we're on the ground. Do not use uncredited stock next to a named family's story."
      ratio="16 / 9"
    />
    <p>
      Damage assessment is slow, boring, and decisive. An adjuster's first number
      is rarely their last one, and the difference usually comes down to what was
      documented and when. If your roof takes damage, photograph it before anyone
      touches it, keep every receipt, and don't let the insurer's inspection be
      the only one on record.
    </p>
    <p class="more"><a href="/help/recover">What to do after a storm &rarr;</a></p>
  </Section>

  <CallToAction title="Are you an organization in the path?" href="/partner" cta="Partner with us">
    Churches, food pantries, senior centres, mobile home communities, clinics —
    you know who needs help and we don't. Tell us who you serve and we'll bring
    what we have.
  </CallToAction>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-sm); margin-top: var(--space-md); }
  .more { margin-top: var(--space-md); font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; }
  .urgent {
    background: var(--color-surface); border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md); border-radius: var(--radius);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .boundary {
    margin-top: var(--space-md); max-width: 56ch; font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-muted); border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding-left: var(--space-sm);
  }
</style>
